1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,624
Why are floating bubbles always round?

2
00:00:02,924 --> 00:00:07,066
Blow through a square wand, and the bubble still comes out round.

3
00:00:07,566 --> 00:00:10,799
A soap film is pulled tight by surface tension.

4
00:00:10,799 --> 00:00:13,826
It always shrinks itself as small as it can.

5
00:00:14,126 --> 00:00:16,476
But the air trapped inside pushes back.

6
00:00:17,076 --> 00:00:21,589
So the film settles on the shape that holds that air with the least surface.

7
00:00:22,089 --> 00:00:23,587
That shape is a sphere.

8
00:00:23,587 --> 00:00:27,822
A cube holding the same air would need about a quarter more film.

9
00:00:28,422 --> 00:00:34,525
Any bulge costs extra film, so the film pulls it back, and the wobbles fade away.

10
00:00:35,025 --> 00:00:36,726
The wand shapes the start.

11
00:00:36,726 --> 00:00:38,428
Physics shapes the bubble.
